\f1\b install:
\f0\b0 \
	$ conda install control-freec\
\

\f1\b config:
\f0\b0 \
	configuration of the tool is done using a Config file\
	has a lot of options including the setting of the required file paths\
	these options are ordered into categories\
[general]	\
	chrFiles:			path to the directory containing the chromosome fasta files\
	chrLenFile:		txt.file containing the list of chromoses with length					or\
					chr_.fa.fai file\
	breakPointType		behavior for ambiguous regions\
	contamination\
	....\
	....\
[sample]\
	here you can either put a bam file or a pileup file\
	optionally, you can also set a .cnp file from a previous calculation for faster computation\
\
[target]\
	same as for sample, but this is the normal control \

